private-warehouse template (private-encrypted tier)

Inherits everything from internal-warehouse with these overrides:

1. meta.yaml.template:
   - tier: private-encrypted
   - trust:
       encryption: age+sops
       key_source: yubikey-primary
       recovery: 1password-emergency
       filename_strategy: ulid
   - federation: lifeops (typical; can override)

2. content/ filenames: ULID-only (not human-readable). Manifest mapping
   ULID ↔ topic lives in manifest.yaml.age (sops-encrypted).

3. pre-commit hook: blocks any non-`.age`/`.enc` file in `content/` —
   PLAINTEXT MUST NEVER REACH GIT.

4. .sops.yaml:
   creation_rules:
     - path_regex: content/.*\.age$
       age: >-
         <yubikey-primary fingerprint>,
         <yubikey-backup fingerprint>

5. GitHub repo:
   - Visibility: private
   - Topic: nexural-lifeops
   - Branch protection: signed commits required

Per THREAT_MODEL §3.3. `nx new <name> --tier=private-encrypted` applies these
overrides automatically + walks Sage through age-plugin-yubikey enrollment.
